#~ can end without returning
# A function that declares a result must produce one on every path.
#
# Without this the compiler fills in a zero, and a function that forgot
# a branch returns a plausible number instead of failing. In a kernel
# that is a coordinate of zero — a point at the origin, which looks like
# geometry rather than like a bug.

fn sign_of(n i32) i32
  if n > 0
    return 1

test "t"
  throw "m" unless sign_of(n: 5) == 1
